course: dictionary
lesson: 12148
title: Words that fit together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compatible means able to work together with something else without problems. «This charger is compatible with my phone» means the charger fits and works with the phone. The clue is work together: two things that fit and work well are compatible.
explain: For people, compatible means alike in some way, so they can get on well. «Maya and Sam are compatible; they both love football and they never argue.» The clue is never argue: they get on well because they are alike.
explain: Ask yourself: do these things fit together and work? Then swap in «fit together and work» and check the sentence still makes sense. Its opposite is incompatible, which means not able to work together or get on.
fact: Compatible means able to work together with something else without problems.
fact: «This game is compatible with my tablet» means the game will work on the tablet.
fact: For people, compatible means alike enough to get on well together.
fact: In medicine, compatible means suitable to be given or put into someone's body without harm.
fact: The opposite of compatible is incompatible.
exercise: «This app is compatible with most phones.» What does compatible mean? | Able to make the phone louder | Too expensive for most phones | Broken and hard to use | *Able to work well with the phone
exercise: «Jess and Ali are compatible, so they always get on well.» What does compatible show about Jess and Ali? | They are both very tall | They never talk to each other | They are always fighting | *They are alike enough to get on well
exercise: Which word means the opposite of compatible? | compact | compatible | *incompatible | complete
test: «The doctor checked that the blood was compatible before the operation.» What does compatible mean here? | Coloured bright red | Painful and very slow | Written down in a book | *Suitable to be given without harm
test: «My new printer is not compatible with my old laptop.» What does this tell you? | The laptop is very fast | The printer is brand new and shiny | They are both on sale | *The printer and laptop will not work together well
exam: «The new game is only compatible with certain consoles, so check before you buy.» What does this sentence suggest? | It is free for everyone to play | It needs no console at all | It is the best game in the shop | *It will work with some consoles but not all of them
